Add a volume API in absolute decibels

The only volume API was `uhda_path_set_volume`, which sets a percentage linearly using the steps
of the audio output's amp. While each step is fixed, the range varies for different codecs. If
a consumer wants to apply their own volume curve (which is our use case), there is no way to do
that without being able to set the volume in raw decibels. On top of that, we need access to the
codec's range as well to calculate the dB value in the curve.

This patch adds:

* `uhda_path_get_volume_range` to read the range of the output's amp as a `UhdaVolumeRange`
* `uhda_path_set_volume_db` to set the volume in decibels, with precision within hundredths of
  a decibel

--- a/include/uhda/types.h
+++ b/include/uhda/types.h
@@ -104,6 +104,12 @@ typedef struct UhdaPathInfo {
 	uint32_t supported_formats_count;
 } UhdaPathInfo;
 
+typedef struct UhdaVolumeRange {
+	int32_t min_cdb;
+	int32_t max_cdb;
+	uint32_t step_cdb;
+} UhdaVolumeRange;
+
 /*
  * Stream parameters
